# Discovery Rules

- Start from user/problem hypotheses, not feature lists.
- Investigate existing alternatives including manual workarounds and doing nothing.
- Separate observed pain from assumed pain.
- Seek disconfirming evidence, not only supporting evidence.
- Personas generated without direct research are hypotheses only.
- Market research must preserve sources and dates for externally sourced claims.
- Discovery outputs should make uncertainty more explicit, not merely make the idea sound more polished.
